  "change_claim": {
    "affected_components": [],
    "architecture_delta": "Harness only: expected_findings in the corpus model, registered facts in grading, the amendment chain in the runner's provenance, and a held-out subcommand. No new dependency; the held-out runner shells out to the system tar for the commitment check and extraction.",
    "contract_changes": "The corpus grading gains registered facts on detect cases, under the DP-1.1c amendment. The checker's CLI and report are unchanged.",
    "intent": "Apply Kennedy's approved amendment after the observed C13 result: register the one accurate warning C13's fixture necessarily produces as a fact, grade registered facts by the every-key rule, re-run H4, and propose crate-level V only if the amended corpus passes. Put the held-out runner Kennedy asked for under xtask, as `cargo xtask corpus held-out`, so the repository keeps one automation home and the tool baseline stays what it is.",
    "non_goals": [
      "Changing checker rules or findings",
      "Changing any other case, cell, witness or grading value",
      "Changing the spec, .rha/policy.toml or the CI workflows",
      "Reading, running on the executor's initiative, or grading the held-out cases (DP-1.1b): the run waits for Kennedy's directory or archive, and the grading is his",
      "Changing Accepted maturity (DP-1.6)",
      "Module-level or transitive implementation"
    ],
    "performance_impact": "none claimed",
    "source": {
      "path": ".rha/tasks/CHG-004.6-c13-registration.toml",
      "sha256": "0786e3f45a09cdbab0c657160522b42c9f83bbef328aa97a1bd2450363991299"
    },
    "task": "CHG-004.6",
    "unresolved": [
      "DP-1.1b: the held-out run waits for Kennedy's directory or original archive; until then the acceptance record and this item say not run, and no outcome is inferred.",
      "DP-1.6: the V proposal for the crate level, if the amended run passes, is Kennedy's to accept, with the post-hoc amendment disclosed."
    ]
  },
